WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.421 --> 00:00:01.350
(tool banging)

00:00:01.350 --> 00:00:02.470
- And that lock is open.

00:00:02.470 --> 00:00:04.100
- [Narrator] Locks like this are no match

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:05.650
for Marc Tobias.

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:06.870
He can easily break in

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:09.240
using a widely available specialty key,

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:10.273
known as a bump key.

00:00:12.117 --> 00:00:13.420
- These are the entire tools that you need

00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:17.980
to open about 95% of the pin
tumbler locks in America.

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:19.413
- [Narrator] So that begs the question,

00:00:19.413 --> 00:00:20.410
(buttons beeping)

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:22.971
is this smart lock the smarter upgrade?

00:00:22.971 --> 00:00:24.620
(keypad beeping)
- [Marc] Open.

00:00:24.620 --> 00:00:26.381
- [Narrator] We put that to Marc.

00:00:26.381 --> 00:00:29.580
He's been breaking into
locks since he was 15.

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:31.530
- In high school, the conductor

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:33.030
of the Denver Symphony got locked

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:33.863
in the dressing room

00:00:33.863 --> 00:00:35.360
and I figured out how to get him out.

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:37.650
- [Narrator] And now he
consults major lock corporations

00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:39.750
in finding security vulnerabilities.

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:42.850
- These companies spend millions
of dollars designing things

00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:44.530
that sometimes we figure out how to break

00:00:44.530 --> 00:00:46.200
in 30 seconds.

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:48.140
- [Narrator] So what
better person to test this,

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:50.090
the Nest x Yale Smart Lock,

00:00:50.090 --> 00:00:51.121
and help us decide

00:00:51.121 --> 00:00:54.506
is it really smart to install
a smart lock in your home?

00:00:54.506 --> 00:00:57.173
(playful music)

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:01.420
The pandemic kept a lot of people at home,

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:04.300
and interested in making
smart technology upgrades,

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:05.810
from thermostats and plugs

00:01:05.810 --> 00:01:07.770
to lights and speakers.

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:10.110
- Everything is moving towards smart locks

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:11.050
in the industry.

00:01:11.050 --> 00:01:12.050
- [Narrator] So that's why we're testing

00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:13.830
the Nest x Yale Smart Lock.

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:15.970
- [Lock] It should be
four to eight digits long,

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:17.530
then press the check to continue.

00:01:17.530 --> 00:01:18.550
- [Narrator] It's a keyless lock

00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:20.570
that can be opened using a passcode

00:01:20.570 --> 00:01:22.687
or when connected to the Nest app.

00:01:22.687 --> 00:01:24.510
- [Marc] And as you see, it turns green.

00:01:24.510 --> 00:01:25.810
- [Narrator] It can be unlocked directly

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:26.993
from your smartphone.

00:01:26.993 --> 00:01:27.826
- Okay.

00:01:27.826 --> 00:01:29.180
- [Narrator] So why did
we choose this lock?

00:01:29.180 --> 00:01:30.450
A few reasons.

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:32.960
It's a collaboration
of two major companies,

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:36.410
Yale, one of the world's
oldest lock manufacturers,

00:01:36.410 --> 00:01:39.860
and Google Nest, a key
player in home automation.

00:01:39.860 --> 00:01:41.910
The lock doesn't have built-in Wi-Fi

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:43.940
but the Nest Connect
system allows the lock

00:01:43.940 --> 00:01:46.010
to indirectly connect to Wi-Fi,

00:01:46.010 --> 00:01:48.700
which the company says saves battery life.

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:50.410
It also has a privacy mode,

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:52.460
which allows you to disable the keypad

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:54.960
so the lock cannot be
opened with a pass code.

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:57.890
The Nest x Yale Smart Lock sells for $279

00:01:57.890 --> 00:01:59.520
with the Nest Connect system.

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:02.450
And $249 without the system.

00:02:02.450 --> 00:02:05.170
Marc is testing the lock
with the Nest Connect.

00:02:05.170 --> 00:02:08.930
- Okay, this must be the Nest Connect.

00:02:08.930 --> 00:02:11.080
We have not had experience
with this lock before,

00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:13.040
so this will be new for us as well.

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:14.670
- [Narrator] First, he
assessed the lock's hardware

00:02:14.670 --> 00:02:16.620
to understand how it functions.

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:18.410
- This is the actual lock.

00:02:18.410 --> 00:02:20.910
It's a brass finish.

00:02:20.910 --> 00:02:23.840
Very neat with a connectorized cable

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:25.590
that goes through the door

00:02:25.590 --> 00:02:27.770
to the back portion

00:02:27.770 --> 00:02:30.543
so that the lock can
talk to the electronics.

00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:33.640
The interesting thing about this lock

00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:35.950
that you'll notice, there's no lock,

00:02:35.950 --> 00:02:38.870
which means it's a
computer-controlled deadbolt.

00:02:38.870 --> 00:02:41.820
There's no cylinder,
there's no bypass key.

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:44.090
Some of the smart locks on the market

00:02:44.090 --> 00:02:46.940
have a cylinder or a bypass key.

00:02:46.940 --> 00:02:48.690
There's pros and cons.

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:51.750
And I should also note that
there's a steel insert,

00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:53.420
a little pin in the middle

00:02:53.420 --> 00:02:57.070
of this deadbolt that makes
sawing much more difficult.

00:02:57.070 --> 00:02:59.280
- [Narrator] Marc's business
partner, Tobias Bluzmanis,

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:03.110
a 40-year locksmith, completed
the installation process.

00:03:03.110 --> 00:03:04.830
- Well, it seems pretty easy.

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:06.210
- [Lock] Installation is complete

00:03:06.210 --> 00:03:07.780
and your lock is ready to be added

00:03:07.780 --> 00:03:08.830
to your Nest account.

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:12.230
- [Narrator] Next, Marc tried
the convenience features

00:03:12.230 --> 00:03:13.270
on his phone.

00:03:13.270 --> 00:03:15.620
- If I hold my finger down on the app.

00:03:15.620 --> 00:03:17.441
- [Narrator] One of them, mobile control.

00:03:17.441 --> 00:03:19.490
(motor buzzing)

00:03:19.490 --> 00:03:21.420
- [Marc] You can hear the
motor drive in the lock

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:25.030
and now it shows me the status has locked.

00:03:25.030 --> 00:03:27.200
- [Narrator] Then Marc tracks
the lock's use on the app.

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:29.002
This is also gonna give me a history

00:03:29.002 --> 00:03:33.870
of every time this lock has
been accessed, locked, unlocked.

00:03:33.870 --> 00:03:35.470
And it'll tell me by whom.

00:03:35.470 --> 00:03:37.320
This is a very clever app,

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:41.000
especially if you have kids,
cleaning staff, gardening.

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:42.730
You send them the code for two hours,

00:03:42.730 --> 00:03:45.880
one hour, whatever the time block is

00:03:45.880 --> 00:03:50.190
and then it'll automatically
cancel after that time block.

00:03:50.190 --> 00:03:52.010
- [Lock] Please try again in a moment.

00:03:52.010 --> 00:03:54.730
- [Narrator] Finally, Marc
gauged the smart lock's security

00:03:54.730 --> 00:03:57.343
and how it compared to
a regular lock and key.

00:03:57.343 --> 00:04:00.470
- This is a standard
five-pin tumbler cylinder.

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:01.580
It's fairly old

00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:04.390
and it's really common
in the United States.

00:04:04.390 --> 00:04:06.210
Honestly, it's a good reason

00:04:06.210 --> 00:04:09.100
to replace this lock with a smart lock.

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:10.267
In less than 10 seconds,

00:04:10.267 --> 00:04:12.573
Marc broke the regular lock open.

00:04:13.627 --> 00:04:14.460
- And that lock is open.

00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:15.532
- [Narrator] Using a bump key.

00:04:15.532 --> 00:04:18.600
- And that's about normal.

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:21.767
- Almost as fast, Tobias is
able to pick the same lock.

00:04:21.767 --> 00:04:23.130
- [Tobias] We got it open.

00:04:23.130 --> 00:04:24.480
- [Narrator] But doing so on a smart lock

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:25.800
isn't as simple for Marc.

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:28.530
- A regular locksmith
can't unlock this lock.

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:32.220
He would have to either drill
it or forcibly remove it.

00:04:32.220 --> 00:04:33.790
- [Narrator] Still, with
a smart lock installed

00:04:33.790 --> 00:04:34.623
on the door,

00:04:34.623 --> 00:04:36.910
it doesn't automatically
mean the home is secure.

00:04:36.910 --> 00:04:40.110
- Of course, the real problem
is there's glass everywhere.

00:04:40.110 --> 00:04:42.450
The majority of attacks on homes

00:04:42.450 --> 00:04:45.400
are against the doors,
the strikes, the glass.

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:46.920
- [Narrator] So after trying out the lock,

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:48.450
does Marc think it's worth the price?

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:52.260
- If you need the option,
it's definitely worth it.

00:04:52.260 --> 00:04:55.930
I would rate it as a five for a smart lock

00:04:55.930 --> 00:04:59.380
with the caveat it's not
a high-security lock,

00:04:59.380 --> 00:05:03.420
and we did not test
the electronic security

00:05:03.420 --> 00:05:05.960
as far as the ability to hack into it.

00:05:05.960 --> 00:05:10.180
Having said that, I would put
this on my condo if I could.

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:12.560
It looks to me like it's
got all the options.

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:14.800
The other thing is you
don't need key copies,

00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:17.620
and copies of keys today can be expensive.

00:05:17.620 --> 00:05:19.870
So is it secure?

00:05:19.870 --> 00:05:24.870
It's probably as secure
as any conventional lock,

00:05:25.330 --> 00:05:28.160
maybe more so because you
can't bump this lock open,

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:30.120
and you can't pick this lock open.

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:33.430
So as far as vulnerabilities
on the mechanical side,

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:35.234
we don't see any vulnerabilities.

00:05:35.234 --> 00:05:37.187
- [Narrator] A Yale spokesperson said,

00:05:37.187 --> 00:05:39.700
"Smart locks do offer an
added layer of security

00:05:39.700 --> 00:05:41.550
over strictly mechanical locks."

00:05:41.550 --> 00:05:43.770
She added, "The Nest x
Yale Lock is compatible

00:05:43.770 --> 00:05:46.150
with most doors with a
single cylinder deadbolt.

00:05:46.150 --> 00:05:47.370
And that the Nest x Yale Lock

00:05:47.370 --> 00:05:49.460
is compatible with most of
the residential market."

00:05:49.460 --> 00:05:51.260
- You need to put the cover back on?

00:05:52.110 --> 00:05:52.943
- Like that?

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:56.163
I'll put the cover on.

00:05:56.163 --> 00:05:58.746
(lively music)

